    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `riskFlag` as a derived, read-only field on the owner response.\n\n`riskFlag` is `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold, else `false`:\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` is true.\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 the stored email's domain shares a known disposable provider's second-level label (e.g. a different TLD like `mailinator.net`, or a subdomain like `smtp.mailinator.com`) without being one of the hard-blocked disposable domains (those are rejected at create time and never stored).\n3. **Over soft capacity** \u2014 `owner.getCapacityWarning()` is true (the warning band starts at the soft cap; since the hard cap of 50 rejects the create, any stored owner over the soft cap carries the warning).\n\nAll three inputs already live on the `Owner` entity, so this needed no pipeline step or DB change \u2014 it follows the existing derived-DTO-field pattern (`contactPreference`, `ownerSegment`).\n\nChanges:\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (drives the generated `OwnerDto`).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 mapped `riskFlag` via `RiskFlag.of(owner)`.\n- `mapper/RiskFlag.java` (new) \u2014 the OR of the three conditions.\n- `mapper/DisposableAdjacent.java` (new) \u2014 exact second-level-label matching for disposable-adjacency (so `tempmailer.com` is *not* matched, only exact family labels are).\n\nThe `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` test confirms a normal owner (no duplicate, no email, unique city) gets `riskFlag: false`.",
